                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "It is important to note that, since OOBNs are composed of a hierarchy of BNs, all their statistical properties, including the chain rule (2), are retained. Moreover, the inference process of OOBNs is particularly efficient in spite of the complex structure since the standard nodes inside an instance are conditionally independent from the rest of the OOBN, given the interface nodes of that instance.",
